  "_what_this_is": "The floor under the clause index, measured from the committed data/clauses.json. Every number was measured, not chosen. See tests/test_index_coverage.py.",
  "_why_pages_are_probes": "The page check used to re-split the PDFs. They are gitignored (data/policies/*.pdf), so the module raised FileNotFoundError nine times out of nine in Jenkins while passing locally - a guard that only ran on the author machine. Each page is now pinned as a 30-character probe: the first line of that page, squashed to bare alphanumerics, that could be found in the index when this was measured. Squashing is what survives join_wrapped_lines. A page whose probe stops being found is a page whose content left the index, which is the only thing this asks.",
